      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/63/1346",
      "text": [
        ": «صَلاَةُ اَلزَّحْفِ عَلَى اَلظَّهْرِ إِيمَاءٌ بِرَأْسِكَ وَ تَكْبِيرٌ وَ اَلْمُسَايَفَةِ تَكْبِيرٌ بِغَيْرِ إِيمَاءٍ وَ اَلْمُطَارَدَةِ إِيمَاءٌ يُصَلِّي كُلُّ رَجُلٍ عَلَى حِيَالِهِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1346 - Ubaydullah ibn Ali Al-Halabi reported from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) who said:\n\"The prayer during advancing combat (al-zahf) is performed on one's back with gestures of the head and the takbir (proclamation of 'Allahu Akbar'). During close fighting (al-musayafa), it involves takbir without gestures. During pursuit (al-mutarada), it is performed with gestures, and each person prays individually as per their situation.\""
        ]
      }
    },
